  "priorExpiration": "2024-07-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 2302.31 “Original loan agreement (OLA)” means the initial financial assistance agreement between the state and a governmental recipient through which the state agrees to provide funds from the CMF to the recipient and the recipient promises to repay the funds to the CMF.\n\nSource. #13858, INTERIM, eff 1-27-24, EXPIRED: 7-25-24\n\nNew. #14078, eff 9-24-24",
